#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:5
#: 7f4bb5215e5b4778a0d4bc652bc6f3fd
msgid "Mission Planner Configuration and Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:7
#: de791063586b478eace194e09a9082bd
msgid "This section of Mission Planner, invoked by the Menu item ``CONFIG`` at the top of Mission Planner, has several subsections. The subsection are where you configure the parameters that control how your autopilot controls your vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:12
#: 39a4627747a2475b9e3a4340192d3846
msgid "Tuning refers to adjusting parameters in the control loops so your vehicle behaves the way you desire. Most of these parameters are set for you when you first install your firmware but some must be set before your first flight or roaming adventure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:15
#: daa44a3c04e245d2b84420afb598e7b9
msgid "What you see when you enter this section depends on whether or not you are connected and which vehicle is connected. Each menu item will bring up a new screen, each is discussed below with links to more detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:18
#: 5defb7ad14544425ac8d5bebfa1d7a86
msgid "Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:20
#: 0e1e105e4af94c8abb14fd8b5688874b
msgid "You will see this menu item if the autopilot is or is not connected. when disconnected, this will be the only active item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:22
#: 4626034d4cbb4b44b60859252c39d355
msgid "This is where you set up most of the options related to Mission Planner appearance and operation. Such things as enabling speech, where the logs are saved, the units of measure you want to use, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:27
#: b3ba2d4f2a76450b91a3f2a79cd4616c
msgid "Flight Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:29
#: 451fa1ba4a13471eb9a1988102da0cb1
msgid "This is where you can set the 6 flight modes controlled by the flight mode channel. This channel defaults to RC channel 8 for Plane, and channel 5 for Copter and Rover, but can be re-assigned by the :ref:`FLTMODE_CH<FLTMODE_CH>` parameter for  Plane and Copter, and the :ref:`MODE_CH<MODE_CH>` for Rover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:34
#: e4963cfff6f047dd861700f45d9d2fbb
msgid "GeoFence (Copter only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:36
#: 4338a65211554936bb0cc1ee216a2115
msgid "This allows configuration of the various Fence/Exclusion Zone/Inclusion Zone parameters. The coordinates of these fences are setup and saved via the PLAN screen. For Plane and Rover, these associated fence parameter must be set manually via the Full Parameter Screen described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:38
#: 000c4333737746fab652e9766537a169
msgid "For more information on Geo-Fences, see :ref:`geofencing`, or :ref:`common-ac2_simple_geofence` and/or :ref:`common-polygon_fence` for Copter and Rover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:42
#: 554ed047446e48d997e4781e0a769c93
msgid "Basic Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:44
#: 2159308347a34bf09f06e44d36ca51f1
msgid "For all vehicles, this shows the relevant basic tuning parameters for that vehicle's attitude and navigation control loops. Read the Tuning section for that vehicle for explanations and instructions on how to tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:47
#: bb072fe8543349a1b5ec7f7a6fff05f7
msgid "Extended Tuning (Copter only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:49
#: cc6def361ecc42fc9dd314a89d357e4b
msgid "For Copter, the Basic Tuning screen is very simple to enable an easy way for beginners to generally adjust roll and pitch tuning. But this screen is similar to the Basic Tuning screen for Plane and Rover, showing the most common parameters for each control loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:52
#: 7e7ac29336f943559efce26de63bcf1d
msgid "Standard Params"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:54
#: 699fbd959071490d83971035ff1c652b
msgid "This screen provides access to parameters that most commonly adjusted by users to alter the behavior of the vehicle for each application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:57
#: 1b4154109ade4d29a9caf4f5b179c2ed
msgid "Advanced Params"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:59
#: 3c4863b5a32e4c89b079a9a56fdb049d
msgid "This screen provides access to many parameters not normally adjusted by the average user, but by more advanced users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:62
#: 220b430578f54fbbaa7caf7e9ee58515
msgid "OnBoard OSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:64
#: af61b8b5ab6d42d7804985e1b0b52f6b
msgid "Some autopilots have integrated On Screen Display (OSD) capability. This provides a means to easily setup the display elements, layout, and parameters associated with these displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:67
#: 7e9dafb58d094017bb36101ac6173a0d
msgid "MAVftp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:69
#: 67065f7977cb404681679e8d78a35425
msgid "In firmware versions 4.1 and later, an integrated FTP (File Transfer Protocol) has been implemented to allow access to the SD card (if the autopilot has one) and internal flash file systems (See :ref:`dev:filesystems`) via Mission Planner. (It is not recommended to use it for log download, use the DataFlash Logs button in the DATA screen, it's faster)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:72
#: 13f667ed5ae34550924b544d77293157
msgid "User Params"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:74
#: 64001f11f1754771b9c80b483bad16bd
msgid "Currently, this allows easy access to setting the :ref:`common-auxiliary-functions` on RC channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:77
#: d5baea95bda445fdbb4b827b83ec33d8
msgid "Full Parameter List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:79
#: e50e69072c3c46bcabe2097ca5e971b2
msgid "Displays every parameter of the connected vehicle. Allows any parameter to be changed and the new value saved (with some minor exceptions for certain read-only parameters). You can also save parameters to a file and restore them from a file, or compare the current parameters to a saved file and decide which, if any to change to that file's list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:84
#: b8da2de41ac9425eb604189de94e04f7
msgid "Load from File: load saved parameters from a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:85
#: 20f7a93c26654e3ba6189b79a74d4fa9
msgid "Save to file: Save parameters to a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:86
#: 490a904e5892469a888c2f732b23373b
msgid "Write Params: Write the modified parameters on this screen to the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:87
#: 55a2319543b344d5bfe28b07c1bf6cd4
msgid "Refresh Params: Reload the parameter list from the autopilot. Often this is required, to display a group of parameters that were just enabled, such when you enable Q_ENABLE (QuadPlane enable mode) on Plane, or a battery monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:88
#: d4e87db450bb4fb48c444526e34f37af
msgid "Compare Params: Compares current parameters on the screen (including modified but not saved yet) to a file, and allows selection of which will be modified to that file's value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:90
#: 16ea346284704606aa0c7984fcbea861
msgid "An important aspect of the Compare Params feature: After you select the file with the saved parameters you want to compare, you will get a window that lists every parameter that is different. At this point nothing has been changed, but if you check some items and then click Continue, those items will be changed in the parameter screen of Mission Planner. You will then need to click the Write Params parameters button in the right-hand panel to copy the changes to your autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:92
#: 8ca1e6f938dd4d02a5659d086b0d54c7
msgid "Load Presaved: Many common vehicle platform typical parameters are available to load via the dropdown box. On loaded, they could be saved to the vehicle with the Write Params button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:93
#: 6aa80cc57e984da887734d57d7ba4345
msgid "Reset to Default: CAUTION! this will immediately reset all parameters to the vehicle's default settings. Recalibration and setup via the SETUP menu will be required or a restore of previously save parameters from a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:94
#: c0e3119d0cd44c0c89006bf16473c303
msgid "Search: Allows a rapid search for parameters by name or included descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:95
#: e536059623fc4ff3bcfe6a2321e04aa2
msgid "Modified: Will display only parameters currently modified and unsaved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:98
#: 640d84e9aa53426db686daee9924b728
msgid "Full Parameter Tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-configuration-and-tuning.rst:100
#: 0cbc5b4208004d56af220ac0146e9929
msgid "A tree style view of the Full Parameter Screen."
msgstr ""
